1
00:00:42,792 --> 00:00:43,877
Sianong!

2
00:00:51,092 --> 00:00:52,218
- Come on, let's go!
- Let's go!

3
00:00:52,927 --> 00:00:53,845
- Ouch!
- Let's go.

4
00:01:06,733 --> 00:01:08,568
Agent Alex, what's the meaning of that?

5
00:01:08,651 --> 00:01:09,861
Is it about Mikoy?

6
00:01:09,944 --> 00:01:12,238
Is that because of them?

7
00:01:16,201 --> 00:01:17,452
<i>At last.</i>

8
00:01:17,535 --> 00:01:19,162
Get inside. We're here.

9
00:01:20,163 --> 00:01:21,915
Take a seat.

10
00:01:21,998 --> 00:01:23,416
Slowly, Angelito.

11
00:01:25,418 --> 00:01:26,920
Drink this.

12
00:01:27,003 --> 00:01:28,004
Thank you.

13
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:32,842
- <i>I want to say thank you.</i>
- For what?

14
00:01:32,926 --> 00:01:34,385
<i>For taking the bullet.</i>

15
00:01:34,469 --> 00:01:36,304
You didn't have to do that.

16
00:01:36,387 --> 00:01:39,349
I did that because you're
a part of our team.

17
00:01:49,109 --> 00:01:50,026
Damn it!

18
00:01:51,194 --> 00:01:52,737
Looks like we got played.

19
00:01:52,821 --> 00:01:54,656
They led us the wrong way.

20
00:01:55,156 --> 00:01:56,741
Come on. Let's go back!

21
00:02:00,912 --> 00:02:02,580
Hey, take it easy.

22
00:02:07,752 --> 00:02:09,838
- Thanks.
- Sianong, the gun.

23
00:02:09,921 --> 00:02:12,090
- Why?
- Brusko, stay there.

24
00:02:13,007 --> 00:02:14,342
- I'll stay here.
- Wait.

25
00:02:35,989 --> 00:02:36,823
Oh.

26
00:02:37,824 --> 00:02:39,534
It's just a wild boar.

27
00:02:42,287 --> 00:02:43,872
What did you say?

28
00:02:43,955 --> 00:02:45,290
Just a wild boar.

29
00:02:45,373 --> 00:02:46,416
A wild boar?

30
00:02:53,464 --> 00:02:55,174
- Yes!
- Yes!

31
00:04:01,491 --> 00:04:02,492
There.

32
00:04:03,993 --> 00:04:05,161
Still nothing?

33
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:07,497
Come on.

34
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:09,040
Unbelievable.

35
00:04:09,123 --> 00:04:12,252
This wild boar you cooked is delicious!

36
00:04:12,335 --> 00:04:15,421
Brother, you're ready to get married!

37
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:19,968
Okay.

38
00:04:20,051 --> 00:04:22,095
Try over here.

39
00:04:22,178 --> 00:04:23,638
I think this is better.

40
00:04:28,977 --> 00:04:30,728
It really won't work, sweetheart.

41
00:04:31,354 --> 00:04:32,188
Come on.

42
00:04:32,272 --> 00:04:33,898
You know what?

43
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:35,984
Let's just conserve our batteries.

44
00:04:36,776 --> 00:04:37,610
Right?

45
00:04:43,908 --> 00:04:44,951
You're right.

46
00:04:45,034 --> 00:04:47,412
And for when someone answers.

47
00:04:47,495 --> 00:04:49,414
So we can keep contacting them.

48
00:04:53,209 --> 00:04:57,672
You know, I can use the car's battery.

49
00:04:58,298 --> 00:05:00,091
I can bypass it.

50
00:05:00,758 --> 00:05:02,885
Not to brag,

51
00:05:02,969 --> 00:05:05,513
but when it comes to technology,

52
00:05:06,014 --> 00:05:07,265
I'm your guy.

53
00:05:08,850 --> 00:05:11,436
Maybe we're just too deep
inside the farmland.

54
00:05:13,229 --> 00:05:17,817
But our biggest problem is the transmitter
and the antenna.

55
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:19,193
Like this one.

56
00:05:19,277 --> 00:05:20,111
It's broken.

57
00:05:20,194 --> 00:05:23,781
No matter how loud you shout,

58
00:05:23,865 --> 00:05:26,117
no one will hear you, Sir Mikoy.

59
00:05:27,368 --> 00:05:29,579
We still don't trust you.

60
00:05:31,998 --> 00:05:33,708
But I want out of here.

61
00:05:33,791 --> 00:05:35,752
Don't you want a signal too?

62
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:15,583
I can't focus
with the two of you staring at me.

63
00:06:16,751 --> 00:06:18,377
It's making me nervous.

64
00:06:21,672 --> 00:06:23,091
We don't care.

65
00:06:23,174 --> 00:06:24,717
That's what I thought.

66
00:06:31,307 --> 00:06:32,683
Can you hurry up?

67
00:06:37,688 --> 00:06:40,483
Hey, are you sure about this?

68
00:06:40,566 --> 00:06:41,400
No!

69
00:06:41,484 --> 00:06:43,861
About 98%.

70
00:06:43,945 --> 00:06:46,364
- Yes.
- You're not helping.

71
00:06:46,447 --> 00:06:49,742
Ma'am, that's pretty high for a tech guy.

72
00:07:12,557 --> 00:07:14,684
Agent Dara, we got something!

73
00:07:57,310 --> 00:07:58,519
Are you talking to that?

74
00:07:59,687 --> 00:08:01,939
Ma'am, trust me.

75
00:08:02,023 --> 00:08:04,650
It's more responsive than most people.

76
00:08:04,734 --> 00:08:06,194
Trust me.

77
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:10,781
Here we go.

78
00:08:35,723 --> 00:08:36,557
We lost it!

79
00:08:39,602 --> 00:08:40,645
Mikoy.

80
00:08:40,728 --> 00:08:42,271
- No, no, no, no.
- Guys.

81
00:08:42,355 --> 00:08:43,272
- Guys.
- Just keep it up.

82
00:08:43,356 --> 00:08:44,941
My armpit is killing me!

83
00:08:45,441 --> 00:08:46,609
Higher! Higher!

84
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:50,947
- Don't move.
- Okay.

85
00:08:54,534 --> 00:08:55,535
Still nothing.

86
00:09:01,624 --> 00:09:04,293
Come on, give me a signal.

87
00:09:04,877 --> 00:09:06,712
Give me a signal.

88
00:09:07,838 --> 00:09:10,550
You said you wouldn't leave me.

89
00:09:11,133 --> 00:09:11,968
Good grief.

90
00:09:12,051 --> 00:09:13,761
Come on, Angelito.

91
00:09:15,096 --> 00:09:17,974
I just went to the bathroom,
and you disappeared.

92
00:09:19,267 --> 00:09:20,434
You're so clingy.

93
00:09:20,518 --> 00:09:22,853
I was just looking for a signal.

94
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:24,981
I was going back anyway.

95
00:09:25,064 --> 00:09:26,649
Go on. Head back.

96
00:09:26,732 --> 00:09:29,360
You might get hurt out there.

97
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:32,363
I'm okay.

98
00:09:33,447 --> 00:09:36,033
You might overexert yourself.

99
00:09:36,117 --> 00:09:37,410
See?

100
00:09:39,996 --> 00:09:41,622
I've already taken my medicine.

101
00:09:42,415 --> 00:09:45,001
See? I'm feeling much stronger now.

102
00:09:47,295 --> 00:09:48,713
Fine, suit yourself.

103
00:10:00,433 --> 00:10:01,809
We will enter here.

104
00:10:03,311 --> 00:10:04,937
Let's head there.

105
00:10:05,021 --> 00:10:08,858
- Yes, just relay it to them as well.
- Thank you, ma'am.

106
00:10:10,901 --> 00:10:13,904
Right. Just let them know too.

107
00:10:16,032 --> 00:10:18,200
Sir, it's Sir Mario.

108
00:10:18,784 --> 00:10:20,244
- Sir Mario.
- Good evening.

109
00:10:24,624 --> 00:10:25,583
Mario.

110
00:10:26,709 --> 00:10:27,710
Norberto.

111
00:10:31,172 --> 00:10:32,757
Let's talk first.

112
00:10:36,010 --> 00:10:38,638
Are you sure you don't
need me for this operation?

113
00:10:38,721 --> 00:10:40,848
Absolutely sure.

114
00:10:41,349 --> 00:10:43,059
We need you at the safe house.

115
00:10:43,142 --> 00:10:45,102
It's important that you're there.

116
00:10:45,686 --> 00:10:48,022
Besides, Tess is probably
worried sick about you,

117
00:10:51,359 --> 00:10:53,778
and I have confidence in Sofie.

118
00:10:54,278 --> 00:10:56,614
They say she's just like me.

119
00:10:56,697 --> 00:10:58,658
Resourceful,

120
00:10:58,741 --> 00:11:03,871
a little stubborn at times,
brave, never backs down.

121
00:11:03,954 --> 00:11:08,501
But as time goes by,
without any news from the island,

122
00:11:09,251 --> 00:11:10,795
I can't sit still.

123
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:14,965
It feels like I can barely breathe
because I'm so worried.

124
00:11:17,676 --> 00:11:19,261
That's how I feel about my sons too.

125
00:11:20,262 --> 00:11:21,806
Even though they're grown men,

126
00:11:22,890 --> 00:11:24,934
I lose all my bravado

127
00:11:26,102 --> 00:11:28,270
when their lives are on the line.

128
00:11:28,854 --> 00:11:34,318
Any father
in your position would do the same.

129
00:11:34,402 --> 00:11:37,446
Whether they've served or not.

130
00:11:40,533 --> 00:11:42,201
Norberto, I know

131
00:11:43,369 --> 00:11:46,580
your priority is to save
your team and Sofie,

132
00:11:48,499 --> 00:11:50,459
but I have one favor to ask.

133
00:11:52,962 --> 00:11:55,464
Bring Angelito and Mikoy home.

134
00:11:56,465 --> 00:11:59,427
They need to make it back safely for Tess.

135
00:12:00,845 --> 00:12:03,889
You have my word. I'll take care of it.

136
00:12:05,516 --> 00:12:06,434
Thank you.

137
00:12:13,524 --> 00:12:14,608
Are you sure?

138
00:12:18,654 --> 00:12:20,197
So it does work!

139
00:12:20,281 --> 00:12:22,074
And you made me climb up earlier.

140
00:12:46,098 --> 00:12:47,141
You know,

141
00:12:48,559 --> 00:12:52,730
I saw the way you looked
at that bomb earlier.

142
00:12:54,732 --> 00:12:56,817
I know how badly you wanted it.

143
00:13:14,585 --> 00:13:16,170
I know you could have.

144
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:19,507
But you didn't.

145
00:13:21,008 --> 00:13:23,761
And I also know the old Chiara

146
00:13:24,345 --> 00:13:26,222
wouldn't have thought twice.

147
00:13:29,141 --> 00:13:31,143
It was easier back then.

148
00:13:32,603 --> 00:13:35,314
Back then, all I worried about
were Mom and Dad.

149
00:13:38,359 --> 00:13:39,860
Things are different now.

150
00:13:45,866 --> 00:13:47,576
Thank you, sweetheart.

151
00:13:53,207 --> 00:13:55,084
But we still didn't win.

152
00:13:56,126 --> 00:13:57,836
We didn't get the bomb.

153
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:01,549
And we still haven't found Angelito.

154
00:14:04,552 --> 00:14:06,679
- Mikoy.
- I found him.

155
00:14:07,179 --> 00:14:09,265
I found my brother.

156
00:14:10,224 --> 00:14:11,934
Then I lost him again.

157
00:14:17,731 --> 00:14:19,942
If I did not leave--

158
00:14:20,025 --> 00:14:21,402
It's not your fault.

159
00:14:22,987 --> 00:14:26,323
It's not Sianong's fault,
and it's not Sofie's either.

160
00:14:28,742 --> 00:14:30,786
We're just having bad luck today.

161
00:14:31,912 --> 00:14:33,247
As salty as the sea.

162
00:14:38,961 --> 00:14:40,713
But we'll find them.

163
00:14:41,547 --> 00:14:43,007
Trust me.

164
00:14:44,592 --> 00:14:46,010
What makes you so sure?

165
00:14:46,093 --> 00:14:47,678
Because I have no choice.

166
00:14:49,263 --> 00:14:53,058
When you're the older brother,
you can't afford to lose hope.

167
00:14:53,809 --> 00:14:55,436
You can't give up

168
00:14:56,645 --> 00:14:58,981
until you know for sure that they're safe.

169
00:15:08,490 --> 00:15:10,367
We'll find them.

170
00:15:13,412 --> 00:15:14,496
All of them.

171
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:21,921
Chiara.

172
00:15:23,088 --> 00:15:24,798
When all of this is over,

173
00:15:25,841 --> 00:15:27,301
I just want to chase children.

174
00:15:31,931 --> 00:15:32,765
Three.

175
00:15:33,682 --> 00:15:35,517
- Three right away?
- Yes!

176
00:15:35,601 --> 00:15:40,940
Just imagine,
two little Mikoys and one little Chiara.

177
00:15:42,024 --> 00:15:42,858
Right?

178
00:15:43,567 --> 00:15:44,735
Wouldn't that be cute?

179
00:15:44,818 --> 00:15:47,071
Why only one little Chiara?

180
00:15:47,655 --> 00:15:49,406
That would be dangerous, sweetheart.

181
00:15:50,324 --> 00:15:53,619
Just imagine,
two troublemakers and one hothead.

182
00:15:53,702 --> 00:15:54,620
Oh, man!

183
00:15:55,245 --> 00:15:56,121
That'd be chaos.

184
00:15:56,205 --> 00:15:58,707
Excuse me. I'm not always angry.

185
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,794
All right, all right.

186
00:16:01,877 --> 00:16:03,087
Two troublemakers

187
00:16:03,170 --> 00:16:04,672
and one…

188
00:16:05,673 --> 00:16:06,590
passionate one!

189
00:16:07,841 --> 00:16:08,968
Better?

190
00:16:10,344 --> 00:16:12,304
You're getting my hopes up.

191
00:16:14,098 --> 00:16:15,015
About what?

192
00:16:15,099 --> 00:16:16,350
That.

193
00:16:17,226 --> 00:16:18,477
Having kids?

194
00:16:27,653 --> 00:16:29,029
Because I want that too.

195
00:16:44,670 --> 00:16:46,005
Angelito.

196
00:16:49,174 --> 00:16:52,720
Do you think they got it?

197
00:16:54,555 --> 00:16:56,098
The bomb?

198
00:16:59,435 --> 00:17:00,602
Maybe.

199
00:17:01,353 --> 00:17:02,563
I guess.

200
00:17:10,612 --> 00:17:12,781
It's not your fault, Sofie.

201
00:17:15,701 --> 00:17:16,827
But…

202
00:17:18,495 --> 00:17:20,164
I just couldn't help it.

203
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:28,881
Sofie.

204
00:17:42,603 --> 00:17:44,354
Thank you for…

205
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:47,900
for staying by my side.

206
00:17:51,904 --> 00:17:53,238
Thank you for…

207
00:17:54,823 --> 00:17:56,617
asking for help.

208
00:18:00,913 --> 00:18:03,916
Thank you for guiding me.

209
00:18:03,999 --> 00:18:05,000
Earlier…

210
00:18:05,793 --> 00:18:06,752
All day.

211
00:18:10,047 --> 00:18:13,383
Thank you for not leaving me.

212
00:18:17,513 --> 00:18:20,474
Even if I was so weak.

213
00:18:28,649 --> 00:18:29,608
Don't mention it.

214
00:19:02,933 --> 00:19:03,934
Oh, come on.

215
00:19:04,017 --> 00:19:05,561
The other day,

216
00:19:05,644 --> 00:19:07,646
I was like your mom, and now,

217
00:19:07,729 --> 00:19:10,232
you're thanking me like I'm your grandma.

218
00:20:06,079 --> 00:20:06,914
Don't.

219
00:20:10,834 --> 00:20:11,835
Sianong.

220
00:20:15,589 --> 00:20:16,757
Sianong.

221
00:20:21,136 --> 00:20:22,012
Don't.

222
00:20:24,139 --> 00:20:25,224
Don't leave me.

223
00:20:28,518 --> 00:20:29,728
Please, don't leave me.

224
00:20:30,229 --> 00:20:31,772
Please don't leave me!

225
00:20:31,855 --> 00:20:33,148
He's burning up.

226
00:20:36,109 --> 00:20:37,402
Believe me.

227
00:20:37,486 --> 00:20:38,737
Sianong.

228
00:20:38,820 --> 00:20:41,698
Believe me, believe me.
I've been looking for you.

229
00:20:43,283 --> 00:20:44,243
I never…

230
00:20:44,326 --> 00:20:45,994
I never got tired of you.

231
00:20:46,078 --> 00:20:48,413
No, I never gave up.

232
00:20:57,256 --> 00:20:58,507
And now…

233
00:21:00,050 --> 00:21:00,884
now…

234
00:21:02,052 --> 00:21:03,303
you're here.

235
00:21:05,639 --> 00:21:09,309
No one will ever separate us ever again.

236
00:21:11,186 --> 00:21:14,189
No one, no one. Stay here with me.

237
00:21:15,983 --> 00:21:17,067
- Sianong.
- My god.

238
00:21:20,988 --> 00:21:21,863
Please, my love.

239
00:21:25,033 --> 00:21:26,285
Can you ever forgive me?

240
00:21:30,205 --> 00:21:31,039
Sianong.

241
00:21:40,007 --> 00:21:43,010
If we stay here any longer without rescue,

242
00:21:44,970 --> 00:21:46,263
he won't make it.

243
00:21:48,098 --> 00:21:49,808
How are we supposed to get rescued?

244
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:52,394
We need to find another way.

245
00:21:53,895 --> 00:21:56,231
We're already struggling to get a signal.

246
00:21:57,357 --> 00:22:00,068
How are we supposed to reach the agency?

247
00:22:01,403 --> 00:22:04,906
If only we had a ninja messenger like W.M.

248
00:22:04,990 --> 00:22:09,244
The one who secretly delivered
the message to Donabel and Viktor.

249
00:22:09,745 --> 00:22:10,954
That was so cool.

250
00:22:11,621 --> 00:22:13,373
So sneaky.

251
00:22:13,957 --> 00:22:15,375
What's W.M.?

252
00:22:16,543 --> 00:22:17,919
W.M.

253
00:22:18,003 --> 00:22:19,421
Winnie the Mooh.

254
00:22:20,422 --> 00:22:21,673
Winnie the Mooh.

255
00:22:21,757 --> 00:22:23,300
Seriously, you've been doing this all day.

256
00:22:23,383 --> 00:22:25,594
Wild boar, Winnie the Mooh.

257
00:22:25,677 --> 00:22:26,803
Will you just shut up?

258
00:22:27,304 --> 00:22:28,138
Especially you.

259
00:22:28,221 --> 00:22:31,183
Shut up with your nonsense
if you're not helping.

260
00:22:31,266 --> 00:22:32,476
You asked for it.

261
00:22:33,310 --> 00:22:34,811
Go get some water.

262
00:22:37,647 --> 00:22:38,774
I know that voice!

263
00:22:42,652 --> 00:22:43,612
Sianong!

264
00:22:44,654 --> 00:22:45,489
Sianong.

265
00:22:52,954 --> 00:22:53,830
Wait, Sofie…

266
00:22:55,540 --> 00:22:56,458
Angelito.

267
00:22:56,958 --> 00:22:58,126
Angelito!

268
00:22:58,835 --> 00:23:00,087
Angelito!

269
00:23:01,046 --> 00:23:02,089
Angelito!

270
00:23:03,131 --> 00:23:04,299
Angelito.

271
00:23:09,888 --> 00:23:12,182
Angelito.

272
00:23:12,766 --> 00:23:14,935
Angelito, not now.

273
00:23:21,358 --> 00:23:22,234
Angelito.

274
00:23:23,527 --> 00:23:24,903
Angelito, wait.

275
00:23:39,626 --> 00:23:42,254
The worst part is we don't have much time.

276
00:23:42,337 --> 00:23:43,839
We can't do anything!

277
00:23:48,593 --> 00:23:50,804
<i>That's not the Chiara I know.</i>

278
00:23:50,887 --> 00:23:54,015
The Chiara I know is always
up to something.

279
00:23:58,103 --> 00:24:00,814
Always mission accomplished.

280
00:24:00,897 --> 00:24:04,359
After all that, she will leave
everything behind.
